# Layer A form of corpus/36-handler-mock-time-now.json — smallest
# Q-030 Handler demonstration. The body calls Time.Now; the Handler
# intercepts and returns a fixed timestamp. By the closure-subtraction
# rule, the surrounding context needs no Time.Now capability.
@v=1 root=handler
intT PRM Int
timeFx EFC "Time.Now"
nowT FNT [] intT [timeFx]
now FN "strand-builtin:Time.Now" nowT [timeFx]
callNow APP now []
fakeT FNT [] intT
fakeLit ILT 1700000000
fakeLam LAM [] fakeLit
handler H timeFx fakeLam callNow
